/**
 * KQuality — Website Chat Router  (n8n Code node "Chat Router")
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------
 * Replaces the old "Build Chat Prompt" node, which sent every visitor message
 * straight to Qwen with a quote-oriented system prompt. Two failures came from
 * that: (a) Qwen runs on CPU at 40-90s/call against a 13s HTTP budget, so most
 * visitors got the generic fallback or a truncated fragment, and (b) the prompt
 * told the model to push the "Request a Quote" button no matter what the person
 * actually wanted — job applicants included.
 *
 * There is no model in this path any more. Every reply is written here, so
 * nothing can be truncated, time out, hallucinate a price, or wander off into
 * a quote pitch. Unclassified messages fall through to a written catch-all
 * rather than to a generation.
 *
 * Every fact below is taken from the live site copy (index.html) or config.js.
 * Nothing here asserts a claim the website does not already make.
 *
 * Output contract: { direct, reply, intent, confidence, service, sessionId }
 * `intent` is returned to the browser so the front-end can route lead capture —
 * a job applicant must never be filed into the quote pipeline.
 */

